WEBVTT

00:00.548 --> 00:03.768
♪ It seems today that all you see ♪

00:03.769 --> 00:07.072
♪ Is violence in movies and sex on TV ♪

00:07.073 --> 00:10.608
♪ But where are those good
old-fashioned values ♪

00:10.609 --> 00:13.645
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:13.646 --> 00:17.148
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:17.149 --> 00:20.518
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:20.519 --> 00:22.087
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:22.088 --> 00:23.455
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:23.456 --> 00:29.927
♪ He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:34.533 --> 00:36.868
Peter, I need you to take
Chris and Meg to school.

00:36.869 --> 00:38.970
Today's the day I finally
kill that squirrel

00:38.971 --> 00:40.972
that's been eating our tomatoes.

00:40.973 --> 00:42.907
Try to get, like, eight
of them this time.

00:42.908 --> 00:44.876
I want to make bruschetta.

00:44.877 --> 00:46.444
Oh, can't the kids just walk?

00:46.445 --> 00:49.381
You know I like to watch two
full movies before I go to work.

00:49.382 --> 00:52.283
No, Peter, they can't
walk, it's three miles.

00:52.284 --> 00:54.119
Fine, I'll take them.

00:54.120 --> 00:55.887
But you better keep those goggles

00:55.888 --> 00:59.057
'cause I'm gonna put them
to good use tonight.

01:01.060 --> 01:02.961
Once the floor is full of sawdust,

01:02.962 --> 01:04.807
we can eat peanuts in here.

01:10.269 --> 01:12.570
Dad, are you sure it's okay
that we took Brian's car?

01:12.571 --> 01:13.772
Yeah, it's his own fault.

01:13.773 --> 01:15.440
He's the one who keeps
his key in the visor

01:15.441 --> 01:17.019
like a carefree hillbilly.

01:17.020 --> 01:18.143
Okay, everybody out.

01:18.144 --> 01:20.744
I don't want the cool kids
to know I'm your dad.

01:23.482 --> 01:24.949
Hey, Chris.

01:24.950 --> 01:27.419
Guess who I just scored as my
date to the homecoming dance.

01:27.420 --> 01:30.054
- Vice Principal McGuire.
- Really?

01:30.055 --> 01:32.123
Yeah, her husband just died of ALS,

01:32.124 --> 01:34.058
so she is ready to get at it.

01:34.059 --> 01:36.327
Hey there, strong guy.

01:36.328 --> 01:38.610
Not now, Brenda!

01:39.465 --> 01:42.901
She says I have the body of a
50-year-old before it gets ALS.

01:42.902 --> 01:44.235
So who are you gonna go with?

01:44.236 --> 01:46.571
I was thinking of asking Kara Morris.

01:46.572 --> 01:48.006
Why don't you ask her now?

01:48.007 --> 01:49.574
Her locker's right over there.

01:49.575 --> 01:51.890
Um... y... uh, yeah, okay.

01:52.511 --> 01:54.446
Hi, Kara.

01:54.447 --> 01:56.815
I was wondering, um, if you'd like to go

01:56.816 --> 01:58.616
to the homecoming dance with me?

01:58.617 --> 02:00.919
<i>Oh, hi, robot from Big Hero 6.</i>

02:00.920 --> 02:03.221
No, but thank you.

02:03.222 --> 02:07.090
His name is Baymax, you gorgeous moron!

02:11.130 --> 02:12.564
All right, red light.

02:12.565 --> 02:15.600
Time to text and shave
and whittle and floss.

02:17.369 --> 02:19.237
- Thanks for getting here so quickly.
- What?

02:19.238 --> 02:20.772
I'm sorry. You're in a Prius.

02:20.773 --> 02:22.474
I just assumed you were my Uber.

02:22.475 --> 02:25.510
I don't know what that is
on account of being dull.

02:25.511 --> 02:27.946
Uber... it's like a cab
except it feels like a game

02:27.947 --> 02:29.113
'cause it's from your phone.

02:29.114 --> 02:30.281
Anyway, I'm late for a meeting.

02:30.282 --> 02:32.350
Can I just give you 20
bucks to drop me off?

02:32.351 --> 02:34.853
Wow, 20 bucks just to
drive you across town?

02:34.854 --> 02:36.488
Maybe I should be an Uber driver.

02:36.489 --> 02:38.323
I mean, I could use the extra money.

02:38.324 --> 02:41.226
And it's got to be easier than
when I was delivering pizzas.

02:41.227 --> 02:42.393
All right, push. Push.

02:42.394 --> 02:43.761
Come on, come on, almost there.

02:43.762 --> 02:45.497
Almost there, just one more push.

02:45.498 --> 02:47.067
Here it is!

02:48.133 --> 02:49.868
Oh, it's half Hawaiian.

02:49.869 --> 02:51.703
I believe that's ours.

02:51.704 --> 02:53.551
You poor fool.

03:00.212 --> 03:01.212
Hey, Stewie.

03:01.213 --> 03:02.547
What's up, big guy?

03:02.548 --> 03:05.316
None of the girls at school want
to go to homecoming with me.

03:05.317 --> 03:08.520
Probably 'cause everyone calls
me names like "Big Nips"

03:08.521 --> 03:11.022
and "Fat Nips" and "Big Fat Nips."

03:11.023 --> 03:13.157
Oh, don't listen to them, Big Fat Nips.

03:13.158 --> 03:14.359
They're just being haters.

03:14.360 --> 03:15.493
What's a "hater"?

03:15.494 --> 03:16.728
Oh, it's just something people say

03:16.729 --> 03:18.879
instead of working to
change their own flaws.

03:18.880 --> 03:20.632
Anyway, you just got to
do what Taylor Swift does

03:20.633 --> 03:21.799
and shake it off.

03:21.800 --> 03:23.667
Who's Taylor Swift?

03:28.407 --> 03:29.607
Oh, my God!

03:29.608 --> 03:32.277
Am I about to introduce
you to Taylor Swift?

03:32.278 --> 03:34.112
W-What is she, a singer?

03:34.113 --> 03:36.314
She's much more than a singer, Chris.

03:36.315 --> 03:38.917
She's... she's... she's the queen!

03:38.918 --> 03:39.951
A goddess!

03:39.952 --> 03:42.453
A gazelle in a high-waisted swimsuit!

03:42.454 --> 03:44.722
Uh, sorry, if you're neither insane,

03:44.723 --> 03:47.659
nor clowns, nor a posse,
I'm not interested.

03:47.660 --> 03:48.927
I have an idea.

03:48.928 --> 03:51.629
You should ask Taylor Swift
to the homecoming dance!

03:51.630 --> 03:54.299
What? Why would she go
to a dance with me?

03:54.300 --> 03:57.068
I'm telling you, this is exactly
the kind of thing she would do.

03:57.069 --> 03:58.836
She's such a sweetheart.

03:58.837 --> 04:00.638
Oh, I'm going limp.

04:00.639 --> 04:03.441
I'm just gonna lie here moaning,

04:03.442 --> 04:05.143
thinking about Taylor Swift.

04:08.013 --> 04:09.180
Tay-Tay.

04:09.181 --> 04:10.748
How would I even ask her?

04:10.749 --> 04:13.084
Oh, it's easy. You and I
will just make a video

04:13.085 --> 04:15.253
about how sad you are and put it online.

04:15.254 --> 04:17.522
She's very interactive
with all her fans.

04:17.523 --> 04:19.051
I guess it's worth a shot.

04:19.052 --> 04:20.058
Of course it is.

04:20.059 --> 04:22.327
If she says yes, you'll
surprise everyone,

04:22.328 --> 04:24.162
just like you did on New Year's Eve.

04:24.163 --> 04:26.698
Three, two, one!

04:26.699 --> 04:28.299
Some animals give me boners!

04:36.942 --> 04:39.177
Hi. Uh, I'd like to be an Uber driver.

04:39.178 --> 04:41.613
Okay, sure. Welcome aboard.

04:41.614 --> 04:44.449
Don't I... don't I need
to fill out a form or...?

04:44.450 --> 04:46.426
Oh, right, yeah, of course.

04:47.319 --> 04:48.620
"Name."

04:48.621 --> 04:50.088
Peter Griffin.

04:50.089 --> 04:51.689
"Criminal history."

04:51.690 --> 04:54.125
This section is optional.
I will skip this.

04:54.126 --> 04:55.426
And done.

04:55.427 --> 04:57.462
Here you go. Yeah, none
of this really matters.

04:57.463 --> 04:59.597
All I need to know is:
do you have a car,

04:59.598 --> 05:01.065
a phone and a face?

05:01.066 --> 05:02.133
It's my dog's car.

05:02.134 --> 05:03.601
Oh, and I know you didn't ask,

05:03.602 --> 05:05.934
- but I am quick to anger.
- Okay, great.

05:05.935 --> 05:08.706
Now get out there and try to
kiss as many ladies as you can.

05:08.707 --> 05:10.408
The record is 60 in a month.

05:10.409 --> 05:12.976
You, sir, are officially an Uber driver.

05:59.032 --> 06:00.291
This is some good stuff, Chris.

06:00.292 --> 06:01.859
I think it's ready to post.

06:01.860 --> 06:04.095
Actually, Stewie, I changed my mind.

06:04.096 --> 06:06.164
I made my own video and posted it.

06:06.165 --> 06:07.732
What? How could you do that?

06:07.733 --> 06:10.268
Stewie, I didn't want to
do all that fancy stuff,

06:10.269 --> 06:13.371
so I just did a video of me
speaking from the heart.

06:13.372 --> 06:15.373
You know, telling her
how much it would mean

06:15.374 --> 06:18.743
if a girl like her went to
homecoming with a guy like me.

06:18.744 --> 06:21.546
I couldn't even stay awake
during that description.

06:23.315 --> 06:25.516
Hey, she already posted a response.

06:25.517 --> 06:27.218
What?!

06:27.219 --> 06:29.020
Hey, Chris Griffin.

06:29.021 --> 06:30.221
I just saw your video,

06:30.222 --> 06:32.256
and I'd love to go to
your dance with you.

06:32.257 --> 06:34.292
All right, I got to go
eat an ice cream cone.

06:34.293 --> 06:36.828
'Cause us stars are just like you.

06:36.829 --> 06:37.829
Oh, my God!

06:39.398 --> 06:43.267
Uh-oh. This means I have an
awkward phone call to make.

06:43.268 --> 06:45.203
What? No, no, it was stupid.

06:45.204 --> 06:47.146
What, two guys going to homecoming?

06:47.147 --> 06:49.340
I-I assumed it was a
goof this whole time.

06:49.341 --> 06:50.475
Take it out.

06:50.476 --> 06:52.459
I'm ugly and unlovable.

06:58.903 --> 07:00.437
Good evening. I'm Tom Tucker.

07:00.438 --> 07:01.805
Our top story tonight,

07:01.806 --> 07:04.240
pop star Taylor Swift
is coming to Quahog

07:04.241 --> 07:07.277
to attend a dance with local
high-schooler Chris Griffin.

07:07.278 --> 07:10.213
But first we go to commercial
while our sports reporter smiles

07:10.214 --> 07:12.315
and spins a football for some reason.

07:17.455 --> 07:19.589
Wow, Chris, I'm so excited!

07:19.590 --> 07:22.025
You actually have a
date with Taylor Swift!

07:22.026 --> 07:24.194
Thanks, Mom. Did I do good?

07:24.195 --> 07:25.829
Can I wear Grandpa's jacket now?

07:25.830 --> 07:27.797
I-I don't know why you
always ask for that.

07:27.798 --> 07:29.966
Th-That's not a thing in our family.

07:29.967 --> 07:31.835
Oh, Rupert, I can't believe Taylor Swift

07:31.836 --> 07:33.837
is actually going to be in our house.

07:33.838 --> 07:35.071
I haven't been this excited

07:35.072 --> 07:36.706
since I abused those caffeine pills

07:36.707 --> 07:38.541
to get ready for the big show.

07:38.542 --> 07:41.211
Everything will be fine, as
long as I take one of these.

07:41.212 --> 07:43.880
<i>Pills? You actually are taking drugs?</i>

07:43.881 --> 07:45.014
Stewie, give me those.

07:45.015 --> 07:46.716
I can't, Zach! I need them to sing!

07:47.885 --> 07:51.688
♪ I'm so excited, I'm so excited ♪

07:51.689 --> 07:55.425
I'm... so... scared!

07:59.597 --> 08:02.698
Screech is going to stab
someone on Christmas.

08:06.737 --> 08:10.240
Oh, Chris, you look so
handsome in your tux.

08:10.241 --> 08:13.176
This must be how Meat Loaf
looked when he went to the prom.

08:13.177 --> 08:15.111
Oh, that must be her!

08:20.651 --> 08:23.052
Hi. You must be Chris. I'm Taylor.

08:23.053 --> 08:24.320
What's up?!

08:25.489 --> 08:27.390
It's so nice to finally meet you.

08:27.391 --> 08:28.958
Your video was so sweet.

08:28.959 --> 08:31.194
And I can't wait to go
to the dance tonight.

08:31.195 --> 08:32.662
Me, too.

08:32.663 --> 08:34.864
Would you like to come in?

08:34.865 --> 08:36.566
Hi. Peter Griffin, leering dad.

08:36.567 --> 08:38.301
Quick question: in "Shake It Off,"

08:38.302 --> 08:42.372
you invite us to get down to,
quote, "this sick beat."

08:42.373 --> 08:44.841
Yet the beat you then
provide is rather mild.

08:44.842 --> 08:47.544
My question is this:
may I lick your legs?

08:47.545 --> 08:49.846
Hi, Taylor. Stewie Griffin.
I'm your biggest fan.

08:49.847 --> 08:52.015
I don't mean that like
a psycho, I just...

08:52.016 --> 08:53.516
I-I'm not, I'm not a psycho!

08:53.517 --> 08:55.218
Oh, you're a cutie.

08:55.219 --> 08:57.353
Okay, so let's talk about Harry Styles.

08:57.354 --> 08:59.022
Now, you don't have to say anything.

08:59.023 --> 09:01.424
I'm just gonna slowly pull
out this tape measure,

09:01.425 --> 09:03.460
and you indicate when I should stop.

09:03.461 --> 09:05.328
Okay, here I go.

09:05.329 --> 09:06.428
Still going.

09:07.431 --> 09:08.998
Still going.

09:08.999 --> 09:11.601
Oh, my God, you bitch! Seriously?

09:11.602 --> 09:15.205
Taylor, this is my sister
Meg and our dog Brian.

09:15.206 --> 09:16.606
Nice to meet you both.

09:16.607 --> 09:18.107
We're not all so impressed.

09:18.108 --> 09:19.909
I've met Dan Aykroyd.

09:19.910 --> 09:23.346
<i>I'm sorry, uh, which cast
member of Hee Haw are you?</i>

09:23.347 --> 09:25.582
Will... you... be... nice!

09:25.583 --> 09:27.917
Okay, well, we should probably go.

09:27.918 --> 09:31.721
It was so nice to meet you all,
except for the girl and the dog.

09:31.722 --> 09:34.257
Sorry about my family.

09:34.258 --> 09:36.326
Don't apologize. They seem nice.

09:36.327 --> 09:39.528
Well, you wouldn't say that if
you ever saw us at the movies.

09:41.832 --> 09:44.067
All right, we got our popcorn from home,

09:44.068 --> 09:46.302
our soda from home, our snacks from home

09:46.303 --> 09:47.637
<i>and Braveheart.</i>

09:52.610 --> 09:54.277
- Where you headed?
- The airport.

09:54.278 --> 09:56.645
Great. Just a couple of errands
and we'll get you there.

10:10.794 --> 10:13.096
That was one bitch of a class.

10:13.097 --> 10:14.497
Anyways, what time's your flight?

10:14.498 --> 10:15.665
It's in 20 minutes!

10:15.666 --> 10:17.600
Oh, boy, I can't make it in 20 minutes.

10:17.601 --> 10:19.035
I better call you a Lyft.

10:19.036 --> 10:21.671
Come on, hurry up, get in!

10:21.672 --> 10:24.140
I hope you like The Offspring.

10:24.141 --> 10:26.709
Let's go!

10:35.853 --> 10:37.854
Oh, my God! Taylor Swift!

10:37.855 --> 10:39.489
<i>She's here with him?</i>

10:39.490 --> 10:40.790
You guys, Mr. Buell's taking

10:40.791 --> 10:43.059
a door-open dook in the bathroom!

10:43.060 --> 10:45.428
I hope this isn't too boring for you.

10:45.429 --> 10:47.664
No, this is so cool!

10:47.665 --> 10:49.098
I always sing about high school,

10:49.099 --> 10:51.067
but I've never actually
seen one in person.

10:52.236 --> 10:53.870
Would you like to dance?

10:53.871 --> 10:55.905
Sure. But you're gonna
have to stand back,

10:55.906 --> 10:58.541
like, five and a half feet.

10:58.542 --> 10:59.676
Cool!

10:59.677 --> 11:03.513
You dance like an unattended fire hose.

11:03.514 --> 11:06.082
Wow! It's like your dance
tells a whole story.

11:06.083 --> 11:07.483
Right?

11:07.484 --> 11:09.619
You are the only one
who's ever gotten that.

11:09.620 --> 11:11.688
Usually people just shove
a wallet in my mouth

11:11.689 --> 11:13.356
and call 911.

11:13.357 --> 11:15.425
You know, Chris, I'm
having a great time.

11:15.426 --> 11:17.660
You're so cool and down-to-earth.

11:17.661 --> 11:19.195
I like you, too, Taylor.

11:19.196 --> 11:20.930
I was scared meeting a celebrity,

11:20.931 --> 11:22.665
but you're so nice and normal.

11:22.666 --> 11:25.368
I feel totally comfortable around you.

11:25.369 --> 11:27.727
Well, why don't you
just kiss her, Griffin?

11:28.205 --> 11:31.358
Sorry, I just smoked a joint
with the pickup truck kids.

11:37.464 --> 11:39.331
That was really fun, Chris.

11:39.332 --> 11:40.850
I hope you don't mind I made the band

11:40.851 --> 11:42.952
pay me a royalty for each
of my songs they played.

11:42.953 --> 11:43.953
Of course not.

11:43.954 --> 11:45.154
And I hope you didn't mind

11:45.155 --> 11:46.956
I showed you who every
locker belongs to.

11:46.957 --> 11:49.292
No, I thought that was nice.

11:49.293 --> 11:50.727
I've never had a locker.

11:50.728 --> 11:54.030
I just keep my stuff in stupid mansions.

11:54.031 --> 11:55.498
Can I finger you?

11:55.499 --> 11:56.633
Sure!

11:56.634 --> 11:58.334
Hi. I'm Taylor Swift.

11:58.335 --> 12:00.670
I'm famous, but I'm really nice.

12:00.671 --> 12:04.374
Aw, that's one of the best
fingerings I've ever had.

12:24.461 --> 12:26.629
What are you working on there, Chris?

12:26.630 --> 12:28.531
Oh, I'm making a collage for Taylor

12:28.532 --> 12:30.600
of some of her favorite things.

12:30.601 --> 12:32.769
Here's flowers and crop tops

12:32.770 --> 12:35.605
and pictures of Kanye
West with his mouth shut.

12:35.606 --> 12:38.753
Wow, you two seem to have
a wonderful connection.

12:38.754 --> 12:39.956
We do, Mom.

12:39.957 --> 12:42.879
You know, she's the first girl
to ever really understand me.

12:42.880 --> 12:44.247
Uh, you guys?

12:44.248 --> 12:46.949
You might want to see this video
Bonnie posted on Facebook.

12:46.950 --> 12:49.052
Why are you on Bonnie's Facebook page?

12:49.053 --> 12:52.121
'Cause she's a (BLEEP) smoke-show.

12:55.292 --> 12:56.926
♪ 'Cause I know you're ♪

12:56.927 --> 12:59.728
♪ Just blubber in a dress shirt ♪

13:02.099 --> 13:04.133
♪ He licked his armpit ♪

13:04.134 --> 13:06.334
♪ Then ate all my dinner and dessert ♪

13:08.605 --> 13:11.274
♪ Chris Griffin is a pig in every way ♪

13:11.275 --> 13:13.710
♪ Oh, oh ♪

13:13.711 --> 13:15.712
♪ Blubber, blubber, blubber, oh ♪

13:15.713 --> 13:17.279
♪ Blubber, blubber, oh. ♪

13:20.751 --> 13:23.853
Oh, and some animals give him boners.

13:28.826 --> 13:30.026
What the hell?

13:30.027 --> 13:31.427
Why would she do this?

13:31.428 --> 13:33.229
Wait, wait, wait.
What's that next video?

13:34.398 --> 13:36.232
Oh, Daughtry!

13:36.233 --> 13:38.567
I'm a mom, so I love this.

13:45.856 --> 13:47.256
Chris, what happened?

13:47.257 --> 13:49.325
I-I thought you said Taylor had
a good time the other night.

13:49.326 --> 13:50.459
We did!

13:50.460 --> 13:52.428
She even let me grab
the part of her body

13:52.429 --> 13:54.230
which on others would be a butt.

13:54.231 --> 13:55.764
Wow, look at these comments.

13:55.765 --> 13:57.132
Everyone hates you, Chris.

13:57.133 --> 13:58.199
She's right. Check it out.

13:58.200 --> 13:59.667
You're already a meme.

14:02.705 --> 14:04.939
Aw, man, Chris, this
computer is telling me

14:04.940 --> 14:06.374
that you done Swifted up.

14:06.375 --> 14:08.866
Why would she do something like this?

14:08.867 --> 14:11.015
Because this is what Taylor Swift does.

14:11.016 --> 14:12.414
She gets into relationship with guys,

14:12.415 --> 14:15.116
sabotages them, and then
writes angry songs about it.

14:15.117 --> 14:16.885
I just wish I could talk to her.

14:16.886 --> 14:19.220
Well, why can't we? She has
a house in Rhode Island.

14:19.221 --> 14:20.221
We could go today.

14:20.222 --> 14:21.856
Oh, my God, we can go today!

14:21.857 --> 14:23.391
My schedule is wide-ass open!

14:23.392 --> 14:25.060
Well, we can't just show up there.

14:25.061 --> 14:27.062
Why not? We've done
crazier things before.

14:27.063 --> 14:29.431
Remember when we sent that tweet?

14:29.432 --> 14:30.731
All right, you ready?

14:34.270 --> 14:35.370
Freeze!

14:35.371 --> 14:36.805
We're the Internet police!

14:36.806 --> 14:39.874
You guys are going away for a long time.

14:40.491 --> 14:42.169
Hey, what are you in for?

14:42.170 --> 14:44.846
I said Caitlyn Jenner
wasn't brave and beautiful.

14:44.847 --> 14:47.915
Brian, there's some bad people in here.

14:50.753 --> 14:53.362
Hey, what's up? I'm just
going to Quahog Stadium.

14:53.363 --> 14:55.853
Okay, would you like the
AC on or the windows down?

14:55.854 --> 14:56.991
How about both?

15:00.396 --> 15:01.896
Pretty great, right?

15:01.897 --> 15:04.231
It is! It really is!

15:07.776 --> 15:09.554
Thank you, genius person!

15:09.555 --> 15:10.437
No problem.

15:10.438 --> 15:13.608
Hey, you ever go in a hot tub
when it's snowing outside?

15:13.609 --> 15:15.809
Oh... What?!

15:20.850 --> 15:23.818
Ms. Swift, your
songwriting team is here.

15:23.819 --> 15:26.087
We got a socko tune for you, Taylor.

15:26.088 --> 15:27.188
Hit it, Morty!

15:28.557 --> 15:31.192
♪ Lox and bagels and bagels and lox ♪

15:31.193 --> 15:33.995
♪ I like being a girl. ♪

15:34.492 --> 15:35.693
Okay, one thought.

15:35.694 --> 15:37.565
What if we change "lox" to "boys"

15:37.566 --> 15:39.534
and "bagels" to "problems"?

15:39.535 --> 15:40.802
Oh, that's perfect.

15:40.803 --> 15:42.806
Like when you changed "pickle it good"

15:42.807 --> 15:43.805
to "shake it off."

15:43.806 --> 15:45.940
All right, we got our homework.

15:46.334 --> 15:47.435
Hi, Taylor.

15:47.436 --> 15:49.750
Chris? What are you guys doing here?

15:49.751 --> 15:51.049
I wanted to talk to you.

15:51.050 --> 15:53.258
Your house is way nicer
than Anne Murray's.

15:53.259 --> 15:54.315
We broke in there, too.

15:54.316 --> 15:56.584
Taylor, why'd you write
that song about me?

15:56.585 --> 15:58.887
I thought we had a real connection.

15:58.888 --> 16:01.442
We do. I really like you, Chris.

16:01.443 --> 16:02.725
I just...

16:02.726 --> 16:04.823
I'm sorry. I always do this.

16:04.824 --> 16:07.493
I ruin relationships with
nice guys and John Mayer

16:07.494 --> 16:10.362
just so I can write songs about
heartbreak and moving on.

16:10.363 --> 16:12.464
But don't you think that's unhealthy?

16:12.465 --> 16:14.333
You're never gonna find
a real relationship

16:14.334 --> 16:15.734
if you keep doing this.

16:15.735 --> 16:17.970
Listen, I'm sorry I hurt
your feelings, Chris.

16:17.971 --> 16:19.571
Let me make it up to you.

16:19.572 --> 16:22.307
Why don't you guys all come to
my show tonight as my guests?

16:22.308 --> 16:23.308
Are you serious?!

16:23.309 --> 16:25.110
Backstage with Taylor Swift?

16:25.111 --> 16:27.679
Well, that'll be even cooler
than when I was in that remake

16:27.680 --> 16:30.249
<i>of The Princess Bride with Bill Cosby.</i>

16:30.250 --> 16:34.253
Now, one of these has the
iocane powder, you see,

16:34.254 --> 16:37.624
and one of them makes you go
sleepy-bye with your mouth open.

16:42.495 --> 16:44.062
Hey, pal, where we heading again?

16:44.063 --> 16:46.063
Just go down this dark alley.

16:53.273 --> 16:54.406
What the hell's going on?

16:54.407 --> 16:57.176
This is what we do to Uber
drivers in this town.

17:01.047 --> 17:02.915
Stop! Stop! Please stop!

17:02.916 --> 17:05.951
The sound of your leather
jackets is excruciating!

17:05.952 --> 17:09.054
You can't just buy a phone
and become a cab driver!

17:09.055 --> 17:11.690
Please, I have two families!

17:16.696 --> 17:17.696
Stay back!

17:17.697 --> 17:19.264
Where-where did you get that?

17:19.265 --> 17:21.300
Judd Hirsch himself.

17:21.301 --> 17:23.735
I was a boy, no more than 11 or 12.

17:23.736 --> 17:25.370
Was on the side of the road.

17:25.371 --> 17:27.105
Man with a hat pulled up next to me.

17:27.106 --> 17:29.541
Said I reminded him of
him when he was my age.

17:29.542 --> 17:31.143
I was just a boy husking corn.

17:31.144 --> 17:32.511
Didn't know what it meant.

17:32.512 --> 17:34.446
Of course, we were all
husking corn back then

17:34.447 --> 17:36.148
just to keep the lights on.

17:36.149 --> 17:38.016
And you burned my car

17:38.017 --> 17:40.953
while I was telling my
fake Judd Hirsch story.

17:52.765 --> 17:55.767
God, I hate everybody
who's not backstage.

17:55.768 --> 17:57.836
This next song is a new one.

17:57.837 --> 18:00.172
It's about my boyfriend Chris.

18:05.278 --> 18:08.247
♪ I'm pretty and I'm
rich and I'm in love ♪

18:08.248 --> 18:09.781
♪ Me Taylor ♪

18:09.782 --> 18:12.217
♪ I've met the guy that
I've been dreaming of ♪

18:12.218 --> 18:13.852
♪ Me Taylor... ♪

18:15.688 --> 18:17.421
Wow, they hate it.

18:19.125 --> 18:20.158
This stinks!

18:20.159 --> 18:22.094
We like you when you're miserable!

18:22.095 --> 18:25.797
You guys, Mr. Buell's taking a
door-open dook in the bathroom!

18:25.798 --> 18:28.467
Why were they being so mean to you?

18:28.468 --> 18:30.502
Well, I guess they're
just used to me being sad

18:30.503 --> 18:31.670
and hurt by men.

18:31.671 --> 18:33.739
But I don't care if they like it, Chris.

18:33.740 --> 18:35.307
I'm happy with you.

18:35.308 --> 18:36.975
I'm happy with you, too.

18:36.976 --> 18:39.144
But it doesn't seem like
your fans like this

18:39.145 --> 18:40.746
new happy Taylor.

18:40.747 --> 18:42.481
Are you willing to risk losing them

18:42.482 --> 18:46.385
and jeopardize your career
and your art just for us?

18:46.386 --> 18:48.720
I think I am.

18:52.732 --> 18:54.760
Oh, well, I don't know if am.

18:54.761 --> 18:57.229
What? What are you saying?

18:57.230 --> 19:00.065
I'm saying that

19:00.066 --> 19:03.302
Taylor Swift, you are a
spoiled ostrich-legged,

19:03.303 --> 19:05.804
no talent, big-footed freak.

19:05.805 --> 19:07.506
You pretend to relate to your fans,

19:07.507 --> 19:09.908
but you make your bodyguards
carry your purse.

19:09.909 --> 19:11.910
All your songs sound the same.

19:11.911 --> 19:14.745
And your cats aren't that cute.

19:19.252 --> 19:21.252
Thank you, Chris.

19:24.624 --> 19:27.626
This next song is about
my dumb ex-boyfriend,

19:27.627 --> 19:29.961
who either mistreated me, cheated on me

19:29.962 --> 19:33.231
or went to massage parlors
when I was out of town.

19:38.980 --> 19:41.640
Wow, Chris, that was really nice of you.

19:41.641 --> 19:43.241
Yeah, I guess.

19:43.242 --> 19:45.310
Don't worry, there'll be
plenty of girls for you.

19:45.311 --> 19:47.646
No one will ever be close
to as good as her,

19:47.647 --> 19:48.914
but we'll find you someone.

19:48.915 --> 19:50.782
What about, like, a motorcycle lady?

19:50.783 --> 19:52.117
You know, like an old gal?

19:52.118 --> 19:54.152
Her grandchildren call
her by her first name?

19:54.153 --> 19:56.142
Let's get out of here.
I called us an Uber.

19:57.390 --> 20:01.063
How many tooths
is not enough tooths?

20:05.665 --> 20:08.300
Well, kids, your father
may have gotten beat up,

20:08.301 --> 20:09.935
but Uber's still a great job

20:09.936 --> 20:11.670
for anyone afraid to sell their blood.

20:11.671 --> 20:13.505
And, Chris, I'm sorry it didn't work out

20:13.506 --> 20:14.940
with you and Taylor Swift.

20:14.941 --> 20:16.641
I think we're all sorry
about that, Brian,

20:16.642 --> 20:18.910
but I'm afraid we are out of time.

20:18.911 --> 20:21.279
I would like to thank our
guests Taylor Swift,

20:21.280 --> 20:23.281
Chris Griffin, Stewie and Brian,

20:23.282 --> 20:26.218
Cleveland Brown and his
band of Brown Renown.

20:26.219 --> 20:28.787
Hey, we'll see you down in
Brown Town, huh, Cleveland?

20:28.788 --> 20:31.123
Oh, I ain't even gonna go there, Peter.

20:32.625 --> 20:34.192
We apologize to the greased-up deaf guy.

20:34.193 --> 20:35.427
Didn't have time for him tonight,

20:35.428 --> 20:37.229
but let's see if we can
get him back next week

20:37.230 --> 20:39.965
when Amanda Peet will be here
with stand-up Dom Irrera.

20:39.966 --> 20:41.333
Good night, everybody.

20:42.836 --> 20:47.927
Thank you for watching "We Bare Bears" on
www.CN-fan.ru